# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ReelForge / Menivor — Railyard RELAY LLM metering (env-gated, OPT-IN)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Route Menivor's LLM calls (script / search-terms / social-metadata generation
# in app/services/llm.py) through Railyard so ALL AI spend is metered and capped.
#
# EVERYTHING here is OPT-IN. Leave these unset and the API keeps its existing
# direct-provider path unchanged (OpenAI / DeepSeek / Moonshot / Ollama / …).
# Implementation: app/domains/railyard/{config,relay,abacus,llm_gateway}.py.

# ── RELAY (TensorZero LLM gateway) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Set RELAY_URL to route OpenAI-compatible chat to ${RELAY_URL}/openai/v1. The
# model id is rewritten to its TensorZero name automatically, e.g.
#   gpt-4o-mini  ->  tensorzero::model_name::openai::gpt-4o-mini
#   claude-3-5-* ->  tensorzero::model_name::anthropic::claude-3-5-*
# RELAY_URL unset  ->  Relay is disabled (direct provider path).
RELAY_URL=
# Optional. gateway.auth is OFF by default, so no credential is needed today.
# If the owner later enables Relay gateway auth, set the bearer token here.
RELAY_API_KEY=

# ── ABACUS (per-key LLM spend caps, optional, fronts Relay) ──────────────────
# Set ABACUS_URL + ABACUS_API_KEY to enforce a per-key spend cap BEFORE the
# request reaches Relay. Point the Abacus deployment's UPSTREAM_BASE_URL at
# Relay so the cap sits in front of the gateway. A cap breach (HTTP 402) stops
# this key's spend (surfaced as RailyardError code="cap_exceeded"); the caller
# degrades to its direct path rather than spending past the cap.
# Both ABACUS_URL and ABACUS_API_KEY are required to enable Abacus.
ABACUS_URL=
ABACUS_API_KEY=
# Per-key identity charged/capped against, sent as `X-Abacus-Agent: agent_<id>`.
# Without an agent id, the Abacus gate is skipped and the request falls through
# to Relay/direct.
ABACUS_AGENT_ID=
